cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PolAgentBench or its published data, please cite the paper below."
title: "PolAgentBench: a Polish-first benchmark for agentic tool use under GGUF quantization"
abstract: >-
  A deterministic benchmark measuring what post-training GGUF quantization does to agentic
  tool use in a non-English setting: Polish prompts against English tool schemas. Three
  models (Bielik-11B-v3.0-Instruct, Bielik-Minitron-7B-v3.0-Instruct, Llama-PLLuM-8B-instruct)
  at six precisions each, over a 67-task main suite and a 46-task arithmetic isolation ladder.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Prejzner
    given-names: Jakub
    email: rd4drop@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/JakubPrejzner/polagentbench"
url: "https://github.com/JakubPrejzner/polagentbench"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - quantization
  - agentic evaluation
  - tool use
  - large language models
  - Polish NLP
  - GGUF

preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    Quantization Thresholds Replicate, Failure Modes Do Not: A Three-Model Study of
    Agentic Tool Use in Polish from 8-bit to 2-bit
  authors:
    - family-names: Prejzner
      given-names: Jakub
  year: 2026
